    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0655" n="1615" xml:id="pg1615"/>

                <head>No. 1095.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 24,
                        1888</date>. (Received October 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 115.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your consideration a copy of
                    a dispatch from our consul at Jerusalem concerning the threatened expulsion of
                    three Jews from Jaffa who arrived furnished with American passports.</p>
                <p>On the receipt of the telegram spoken of by Mr. Gillman, I had requested the
                    sending of a telegram by the minister of foreign affairs, and later (September
                    8) of another by the Grand Vizier, which I hope stopped the efforts to expel
                    them. I have asked the consul-general for information about the present state of
                    the matter.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of my note to the Porte on the subject, which I hope will meet
                    your approval.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton King</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d382-a1.xml" xpointer="d382-a1"/>
